                            # So conflict if there exists a neighbor u of v such that:
                            #   (color[u] == target_color and after swap becomes c) -> conflict if v gets c
                            #   or (color[u] == c and after swap becomes target_color) -> no conflict for v getting c
                            # Actually, we only care about neighbors ending up with color c after swap.
